  <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 50px;">Instructions for Students Registering on College Central at NJCU</h2>

  <p style="margin-top: 30px;">College Central is New Jersey City University's online page through which seniors and graduates can post resumes & cover letters, view job openings posted with the Career Center and submit resumes to employers via the internet. To register on College Central at NJCU take the following steps:</p>

  <ol style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <li>Go to the Career Center website at <span data-field="website_url">{{ website_url }}</span></li>
    <li>Click on either the “Undergraduates” or “Graduate Students” menu option.</li>
    <li>Scroll down and click on “College Central” (All the College Central links are the same)</li>
    <li>On the “Welcome” page scroll down and click on the “student” option.</li>
    <li>On the “Student Services” page scroll down and click on the “Create account” link (or go to “Sign In” to access the site after you have registered and enter your access ID and password).</li>
    <li>Create your own ID and case sensitive password on the “Student Services” page. If you are registering, your user ID is your Gothic ID number preceded by zeros to total nine digits.</li>
    <li>Click “Continue”.</li>
    <li>Complete the registration information and click “submit information”.</li>
    <li>Problems with registering on or navigating NJCU College Central: contact the Career Center at 201-200-2181 or <span data-field="support_email">{{ support_email }}</span>.</li>
  </ol>
</div>

